    "result_text": "Full suite is green: **34 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nReplaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133), computed at read time as `1 + (email present) + (namesakeCount == 0)`, capped at 3. Four files changed:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Removed the `String getMembershipTier()` derived getter (with its `GOLD`/`SILVER`/`BRONZE` + household-size logic) and replaced it with `Integer getMembershipLevel()`: starts at 1, adds 1 for a present email, adds 1 when `namesakeCount` is 0, capped at 3 (leaving level 4 reserved for tenure). Household size no longer feeds the level.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Renamed the response schema property `membershipTier` \u2192 `membershipLevel`, changed it to `integer`/`int32` with `minimum: 1`, `maximum: 3`. This regenerates the DTO field, and MapStruct's implicit name-matched mapping follows automatically. The old string field is gone from the response.\n\n3. **`AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 The create audit line now records `membershipLevel={}` alongside the owner id (previously it recorded neither a tier nor a level; the spec requires the level be recorded there).\n\n4. **`AssignHouseholdSize.java`** \u2014 Updated the stale javadoc that referenced the removed `getMembershipTier()`/GOLD behaviour.\n\nThe relevant acceptance tests (Cp15 \u2192 level 3, Cp21 \u2192 audit line contains the level, Cp23 \u2192 level 2 with no GOLD tier, Cp24 \u2192 capped at 3) and the full suite all pass.",
